; A string is a String and an integer is an Int - the fiat that
; unified them BY NAME in tyCompat was deleted on 2026-08-15, after a
; campaign took the fiat-off error count to zero for the compiler,
; the stdlib, and the corpus. Three shapes it used to accept, each
; now the plain AX3004 it always deserved:
;
;   line 27: arithmetic on a string - `(+ 1 "hi")` added one to an
;            address for as long as the language existed
;   line 28: a string into an Int-declared parameter
;   line 29: an integer into a String-declared parameter
;
; String EQUALITY is untouched: `==` on two Strings answers Bool
; through the content rewrite (035-string-equality pins it).
; The pre-deletion compiler accepts this whole file, exit 0.
(:: addOne (-> Int Int))

(fn (addOne n) (+ n 1))

(:: shout (-> String String))

(fn (shout s) s)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  {
    (+ 1 "hi")
    (addOne "three")
    (shout 42)
    0
  }
)
